;; The sha is the RATCHET: coverage floors measured against one loader do
;; not carry to another, so changing tools/kexe_loader.c must fail here
;; until someone decides what the floors are for the new one.
;;
;; Advanced 2026-09-09 for the granted-region argument forms (`g:<hex>`
;; and `gl:<n>`), the report tail, and the pool-is-last assert.
;;
;; Advanced 2026-09-15 for the buffered wire 37, the CPU/wall budgets, the
;; arena ceilings, the browse entry bound, the ABI v5 string_index_of slot
;; and the string-concat tail append; and 2026-09-16 for the ABI v6
;; arena-scope pair, which the handle-graph target now reaches unpaired;
;; and again 2026-09-16 for the ABI v7 text slots (string_compare,
;; string_fold_ascii, string_find_blank, string_skip_blank; the
;; handle-graph target reaches all four) and the memchr-first memmem
;; behind string_index_of; and again 2026-09-16 for the ABI v8 line slots
;; (string_index_of_from, string_compare_lines; the handle-graph target
;; reaches both) and the hand-written decimal in the write provider; and
;; once more 2026-09-16 for the vector arenas as per-run budgets
;; (KEXE_VECTORS / KEXE_VECTOR_ITEMS, mmap'd maxima) and the per-vector
;; limit 2^24, the one-pass string_compare_lines and string_concat
;; validating its inputs; and for context ABI v9 (six data pointers the
;; compiler's inline handle operations read; nothing new in the C surface
;; the fuzzer drives) -- none of which touches the argv/handle parser the
;; floors measure. The floors are again carried
;; forward unmeasured, for the same reason as below.
;;
;; ⚠ THE FLOORS BELOW WERE NOT RE-MEASURED. They are the previous
;; loader's, carried forward, and that is stated rather than implied:
;; libFuzzer's runtime (libclang_rt.fuzzer_osx.a) is not installed on
;; the machine that made this change, so `npm run fuzz` there takes the
;; deterministic-sanitized arm and never reaches this file. The Linux CI
;; job is what measures them. The change ADDS parser branches rather
;; than removing any, so the floors should be met or exceeded -- but
;; "should" is the word, and if CI reports higher numbers these floors
;; are now looser than the code deserves and should be raised.
;; Advanced 2026-09-18 for wire 42 (:gpu/compute): the guest-side provider
;; (a length-framed request over a pipe, the answer interned), the
;; supervisor-side broker in supervise() (poll on the request pipe until the
;; guest closes it), the pipe pair minted before fork when the grant names
;; 42, and `read` admitted under the sandbox while the broker is active. The
;; Vulkan mechanism itself is tools/kexe_gpu_vulkan.c, included only under
;; -DKEXE_GPU_VULKAN, so this sha covers the loader and not the driver-side
;; module (root ADR-2609182400 C). Advanced again 2026-09-19 for the ordered
;; Vulkan teardown call at the end of the broker loop (amu #1028).
;;
;; Advanced 2026-09-19 for arena_exhausted: the parser is untouched, so this
;; is the ratchet doing its bookkeeping rather than reporting a new surface.
;; The floors are again NOT re-measured, for the same reason as above, and
;; the change adds no parser branch at all -- the new code runs only on
;; paths that were already about to raise(SIGILL).
;;
;; Advanced 2026-09-24 for adr-2609242100 P1 (kotoba-lang lang/limits.edn):
;; KEXE_RECORD_FIELD_LIMIT 128 -> 32 and the KEXE_FUEL ceiling 2^53-1. The
;; first DOES touch the argv parser -- an `r:` record argument is refused at
;; its 33rd field instead of its 129th -- but only moves the threshold of an
;; existing branch, adding none; the second runs before the guest starts.
;; The floors are carried forward NOT re-measured (same machine limitation
;; as above); the Linux CI fuzz job measures them.
;; Advanced 2026-09-24 for wire 2 (:identity/verify): an Ed25519 verifier
;; (verify only, no secret) and its provider, reached only through a granted
;; cap_call -- the argv/handle parser the floors measure is untouched, and
;; the new request parser (four decimals) runs only inside the provider. The
;; floors are carried forward NOT re-measured, same machine limitation as
;; above; the Linux CI fuzz job measures them.
;; Advanced 2026-09-24 for adr-2609242100 P4: fuel unmetered by default
;; (KEXE_FUEL=n / off), budget_exhausted recorded by the refusing host calls
;; and named by the supervisor (report_budget_trap), and the alternate-stack
;; SIGSEGV/SIGBUS handler that names :host/stack-exhausted. The argv/handle
;; parser is untouched; floors carried forward NOT re-measured (same machine
